# Mentor Pro scheduled replenishment (T066). User crontab of the deploy user (docker group); no root needed.
# Install (once): install -m 700 -D deploy/mentorpro-replenish-tick.sh $HOME/mentor-pro-review/bin/mentorpro-replenish-tick.sh
#   then $HOME/mentor-pro-review/bin/mentorpro-replenish-tick.sh --check (creates the log dir, checks the container),
#   then crontab -l | cat - deploy/mentorpro-replenish.cron | crontab -   (check with crontab -l)
# Remove:  crontab -l | grep -v mentorpro-replenish | crontab -
# The tick does nothing until MENTOR_PRO_REPLENISH_SCHEDULE=on in the app environment; pause at any time with
# `docker exec mentor-pro-app-1 python -m app.practice.replenish pause --reason ...`.
# Every 3 hours at :17, at most MENTOR_PRO_REPLENISH_TICK_CALLS free calls per tick (default 10, so <= 80/day),
# inside the shared daily budget. One line per tick in the log; details in generation.replenish_tick.
# The wrapper logs one RESULT=... line per tick (OK, SKIPPED, TICK_FAILED, ERROR, CONTAINER_MISSING, DOCKER_ERROR,
# LOG_ERROR), redacts secrets, and exits with the real status. See runbook section M.
17 */3 * * * $HOME/mentor-pro-review/bin/mentorpro-replenish-tick.sh # mentorpro-replenish
